The bug was caused by a signed/unsigned integer mismatch in the calculation of the timestamp adjustment in the `stmmac_get_tx_hwtstamp` function. The variable `adjust` was defined as a signed 64-bit integer (`s64`), but the addition operation involved an unsigned 64-bit integer (`u64 ns`). This led to incorrect behavior on 32-bit systems, where the compiler treated the addition as a `u64 + u32`, resulting in an off-by-error in the timestamp calculation. The RX function avoided this issue by using an unsigned 64-bit variable for adjustment, but the inconsistency in handling the adjustment logic between the two functions was problematic.

